  "You and Kavya ended it in the year that tested everyone. Nobody shouted. Nobody posted anything. You said thank you, and meant it.\nA year later she sends a photo from her athletics scholarship. You send one back from your own first real step with {passion}. You're both, quietly, better people than the two kids who met in JC1.\nMochi: \"Ending well is still love. You lost a girlfriend, not yourself.\"": "在那个考验每个人的一年，你和卡维娅分开了。没有人大吵。没有人发帖。你说了谢谢，而且是真心的。\n一年后，她传来一张她的田径奖学金的照片。你回传一张你在{passion}上踏出第一步的照片。你们两个都悄悄地，比当年初院一年级认识的那两个小孩更好了。\n麻糬：“好好结束，也是爱。你失去的是女朋友，不是你自己。”",
  "A few years after the A-levels. Elise is deep into her dance academy in Seoul. You're deep into {passion}, your course and your own plans. Neither of you shrank to fit the other.\nYou still meet at a quiet table at a hawker centre, no camera. You still argue sometimes, and fix it before it sets. You know her real favourites now, not the ones you guessed.\nOn your desk: a photo that was never posted, just printed and kept. On her phone: a budget you made together. It balances.\nMochi, from the windowsill: \"Not fireworks. A fire you both keep lit. The good kind.\"": "A水准考完几年后。伊莉丝在她在首尔的舞蹈学院里忙得不得了。你忙着{passion}、你的课和你自己的计划。你们谁都没有为了迁就对方把自己缩小。\n你们还是会在小贩中心一张安静的桌子，没有镜头见面。有时还是会吵，但会在变成心结之前讲开。你现在知道她真正喜欢什么，不是你以前猜的那些。\n你的桌上：一张从没上传过的照片，只是洗出来收着。她的手机里：一份你们一起做的预算。收支平衡。\n麻糬在窗台上说：“不是烟火。是一把你们一起顾着的火。好的那种。”",
